    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17672" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fămŭlātus</span></b> ,
			ūs, m.
		famulor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>servitude</i>, <i>slavery</i> (rare
			but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in famulatu esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Lael. 19, 70</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quam miser virtutis famulatus servientis
					voluptati!</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Off. 3, 33, 117</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gravis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Hippol. 991</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in famulatum subeunte natura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 1, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Exod. 1, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
